			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Stormwind City is the capital of the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link} and the greatest city of {link:humans}humankind{/link} still standing in the south. Its white walls rise at the western edge of {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn Forest{/link}, and blue canals run between its districts. Merchants crowd the {link:trade-district}Trade District{/link}. Pilgrims climb the steps of the {link:cathedral-of-light}Cathedral of Light{/link}. Above them all stands {link:stormwind-keep}Stormwind Keep{/link}, where the kings of the realm have ruled for generations. The city is proud, rich and crowded. It is also a city without its king.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records the year Stormwind was founded. Its roots lie with the families of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} who travelled south long ago and raised a kingdom they named {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}. Stormwind was its heart. For centuries the city grew in peace, and the Church of the {link:holy-light}Holy Light{/link} made it one of the great seats of its faith. Then came the {link:first-war}First War{/link}. The orcish {link:horde}Horde{/link} burned the kingdom and sacked the capital, and King {link:llane-wrynn}Llane Wrynn{/link} died within his own keep. The survivors fled north with Sir {link:anduin-lothar}Anduin Lothar{/link} to {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Stormwind was raised again after the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, stone by stone, by the {link:stonemasons-guild}Stonemasons' Guild{/link}. When the {link:house-of-nobles}House of Nobles{/link} refused to pay for that labor, the masons rioted, Queen {link:tiffin-wrynn}Tiffin Wrynn{/link} was killed, and the masons were driven out. They became the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias Brotherhood{/link}.

Now King {link:varian-wrynn}Varian Wrynn{/link} has vanished on a diplomatic journey, and no one at court can say where he is. His young son {link:anduin-wrynn}Anduin{/link} holds the title of king. Highlord {link:bolvar-fordragon}Bolvar Fordragon{/link} rules in his name as regent, and the noblewoman {link:katrana-prestor}Katrana Prestor{/link} is often at his side. The army is far away. The Defias prey on the roads outside the walls. Inside the walls, the prisoners of the {link:the-stockade}Stockade{/link} have risen against their guards. The agents of {link:si-7}SI:7{/link} suspect that someone at court is helping the Brotherhood.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The people of Stormwind.{/b} Merchants, craftsmen, sailors, clerks and the refugees of the wars.
• {b}The court and the nobles.{/b} The regent, his counsellors and the lords of the {link:house-of-nobles}House of Nobles{/link} gather in {link:stormwind-keep}Stormwind Keep{/link}.
• {b}The clergy.{/b} The priests and paladins of the {link:cathedral-of-light}Cathedral of Light{/link} serve under {link:archbishop-benedictus}Archbishop Benedictus{/link}.
• {b}The dwarves of Ironforge.{/b} They keep their own quarter by the city walls, with its forges and the tunnel to {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}.
• {b}The mages.{/b} The wizards of the {link:mage-quarter}Mage Quarter{/link} study and teach within sight of the Keep.
• {b}Hidden folk.{/b} {link:si-7}SI:7{/link} works from the shadows of {link:old-town}Old Town{/link}. Warlocks gather in the cellar of a tavern, and few folk ask what they do there.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Old Kingdom.{/b} For centuries Stormwind was the capital of a peaceful realm, ruled by the house of Wrynn.
• {b}The Fall.{/b} In the {link:first-war}First War{/link} the {link:horde}Horde{/link} breached the city. {link:llane-wrynn}Llane{/link} was slain and his son {link:varian-wrynn}Varian{/link} was carried into exile.
• {b}The Rebuilding.{/b} After the {link:second-war}Second War{/link} the exiles came home, and the masons rebuilt the city on its old foundations.
• {b}The Riot.{/b} The nobles would not pay the masons. The quarrel ended in blood, and in the death of the queen.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The king is missing. A child sits on the throne, a regent governs, and the kingdom's enemies grow bold at home.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the City",
			text = [=[• The new Stormwind was built on the ruins of the old. Many of the men who raised its walls now hide among the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias{/link}.
• A cheesemonger in the {link:trade-district}Trade District{/link} is not only a cheesemonger. Those who know which door to use say that {link:si-7}SI:7{/link} keeps an eye on the city from his shop.
• Ships now sail from a new harbor on the city's western shore across the sea to {link:auberdine}Auberdine{/link} in {link:darkshore}Darkshore{/link}.]=],
